0 Pileipellis a tangled cutis of mainly hyaline to  faintly yellow hyphae 7-15 µm  broad;  pileus pale cream-orange to bright yelloworange  or orange, surface felty; lamellae pale  to dark orange; spores 5.5-7 x 3-4 µm ,  ellipsoid to distinctly cylindric, weakly  dextrinoid ; in mixed woods, open heaths or  grassland 045816110 H. aurantiaca0
0 Pileipellis with trichodermal tufts of erect  hyphae, some broad, thick-walled and hyaline,  some with granular golden-brown contents,  others filiform; pileus with dark brown velvet    hairs faintly to densely covering a paler, more  orange ground; lamellae from pale creamsalmon  to deep orange; spores 6-7 x 3-4(-4.5)  µm , ellipsoid to slightly cylindric, strongly  dextrinoid; usually on or around conifer  stumps or on wood chips 045916120 H. rufa0
